# Scroll Features Reference — ScrollStudio Pattern

Reverse-engineered from example-studio.com/work/sample-scroll-project

---

## Dependencies

- **Lenis** (v1.0.27) — smooth scroll engine via `@studio-freight/react-lenis`
- **GSAP** + **ScrollTrigger** + **CustomEase** — scroll-driven animations
- **Next.js** — framework (page-level orientation switching)

---

## 1. Horizontal Scroll

Lenis is configured globally with orientation switching per page type.

### Lenis Config

```js
const lenisOptions = {
  duration: 1.3,
  easing: (t) => Math.min(1, 1.001 - Math.pow(2, -10 * t)),
  wheelMultiplier: 1.4,
  orientation: page.type === "work_item" ? "horizontal" : "vertical",
  gestureOrientation: page.type === "work_item" ? "both" : "vertical",
};
```

- `orientation: "horizontal"` makes Lenis scroll the page left/right
- `gestureOrientation: "both"` allows both swipe directions to trigger horizontal scroll (important for trackpads/touch)

### Sync GSAP ticker with Lenis

```js
useEffect(() => {
  if (!lenis) return;
  ScrollTrigger.refresh();
  gsap.ticker.remove(gsap.updateRoot);
  raf.add((time) => {
    gsap.updateRoot(time / 1000);
    lenis.raf(time);
  });
}, [lenis]);
```

### Layout CSS

```css
.workItemFlex {
  display: inline-flex;
  column-gap: 1.39rem;          /* ~20px scaled */
  height: 100vh;
  height: 100svh;
}

.workItemFlex > * {
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* Fixed black background behind everything */
.bg {
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  width: 100vw;
  height: 100vh;
  background-color: #000;
  z-index: -11;
}
```

Key: `inline-flex` + `flex-shrink: 0` on children creates a naturally wide container. Lenis scrolls it horizontally.

### Mobile fallback (<=480px)

```css
@media screen and (max-width: 480px) {
  .workItemFlex {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    height: auto;
  }
}
```

---

## 2. Gradient Rise + Text Reveal

The hero section is `200vw` wide. As you scroll through it horizontally, two things animate via ScrollTrigger with `scrub`:

### Hero CSS

```css
.header {
  position: relative;
  width: 200vw;
  height: 100vh;
  overflow-y: clip;
}

.gradient {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  transform: scaleY(0);
  transform-origin: bottom;
  background: linear-gradient(0deg, #000, transparent);
}

.titleWrap {
  position: sticky;
  left: 1.39rem;
  bottom: 50%;
  width: 50rem;
  color: #fff;
  mix-blend-mode: difference;
  transform: translate3d(0, 50%, 0);
}

.grid {
  position: sticky;
  bottom: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100vw;
  color: #fff;
  mix-blend-mode: difference;
  transform: translate3d(0, 100%, 0);   /* starts off-screen below */
}
```

### GSAP Animations

```js
useEffect(() => {
  if (window.innerWidth <= 480) return;

  const ctx = gsap.context(() => {
    // Gradient scales up from bottom
    gsap.to(gradientRef.current, {
      scrollTrigger: {
        horizontal: true,
        trigger: headerRef.current,
        scrub: true,
        start: "left left",
        end: "right right",
        invalidateOnRefresh: true,
      },
      scaleY: 1,
    });

    // Info grid slides up into view
    gsap.to(gridRef.current, {
      scrollTrigger: {
        horizontal: true,
        trigger: headerRef.current,
        scrub: true,
        start: "left left",
        end: "right right",
        invalidateOnRefresh: true,
      },
      y: 0,
    });
  });

  return () => ctx.revert();
}, [gridRef, headerRef]);
```

Both use `scrub: true` so they follow scroll position exactly (no play/pause).

---

## 3. [SCROLL] Progress Indicator

A fixed bottom bar with tick marks and a draggable `[SCROLL]` handle.

### Structure

```
scrollWrap (fixed, bottom: 0, starts at translateY(50vh))
  scroll (sticky, flex, space-between)
    div × 28 (tick marks)
    scrollHandle (absolute, translateX based on progress)
      brackets (two SVG bracket icons [ ])
      span "SCROLL"
```

### CSS

```css
.scrollWrap {
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 0;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  padding: 1.67rem 0;
  transform: translateY(50vh);          /* hidden below, animated to y:0 */
  z-index: 3;
  user-select: none;
}

.scroll {
  position: sticky;
  left: 0;
  width: 100vw;
  padding: 0 3.47rem;                  /* ~50px scaled */
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
}

/* Tick marks */
.scroll div:not(.scrollHandle) {
  width: 0.14rem;                       /* ~2px */
  height: 0.83rem;                      /* ~12px */
  background: #323232;
}

/* Handle */
.scrollHandle {
  position: absolute;
  top: -0.28rem;
  left: 0;
  color: #fff;
  cursor: grab;
}

.brackets {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  width: 6.94rem;                       /* ~100px */
  height: 1.39rem;                      /* ~20px */
  background: #000;
  transition: transform 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1);
}

.scrollHandle.handleDown {
  cursor: grabbing;
}

.scrollHandle.handleDown .brackets {
  transform: scale(1.2);
}
```

